WEBVTT

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:02.870
I withdraw.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.610
What are you saying?

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:08.980
I don't want to anymore. That's what I've decided.

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.190
I'll tell Kanazawa-sensei.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.890
Hey, what's the meaning of this?

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:15.860
Hey, Hino!

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.450
You have nothing to do with it, Tsuchiura-kun!

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.420
Yes I do!

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.730
It's because you were there that I...

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:09.060
Pavane for a Lost Heart.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.110
This is the school daily records.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.430
Thank you, good job.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.870
Pardon me.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:28.140
I said that to Tsuchiura-kun yesterday, but...

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.430
Well you see, it's just so sudden...

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:50.550
I apologize for informing you like this.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.690
You don't have to be so formal about it.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.820
It's a decision you've thought long and hard about, right?

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:00.320
Well, as long as it's something you've decided for yourself...

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.850
Thank you very much.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:08.770
As soon as things are formalized, I'll visit you once again.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.610
This-This isn't good!

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.710
I'm thinking of just going straight home today.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.260
Yeah, sounds like a plan.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.800
This is an important time for Kaho-chan, right?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.980
Huh? Isn't that?

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.540
I haven't heard anything about what he said, no way!

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.700
You're Fuyuumi-san, right?

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.440
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.440
Um, is Kaho-sempai around?

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.990
Kaho said she had something to do.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.490
Something to do?

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:49.870
So then, is she playing the violin again?

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.000
No, I don't think so. She didn't bring her violin again today.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.940
I see.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.360
It's simple, really.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:09.990
I'll go to Kanazawa-sensei's office, and say "I withdraw from the competition."

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:14.790
Because I have no right to play the violin.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:20.100
And yet, why was I so relieved that he wasn't there?

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.930
What's the matter?

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:29.220
You're acting like some wilted flower talking to herself with her head hung low...

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:30.700
Yunoki-sempai.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.840
Then just leave me alone.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.750
Can't do that, can I?

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:40.750
When I see a wilted flower, it makes me want to water it.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:42.760
What are you...

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.570
Don't take me so seriously.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:52.930
I have confidence in myself, see. When it comes to flowers, actually plucking one is...

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:02.540
You look like you want to throw away everything and just run away.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.870
I'll be studying abroad at a school in England soon.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.580
When I go, would you come with me?

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:21.810
I'll take you with me if you want me to.

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.440
What... What are you saying?

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:29.110
Studying abroad? What about the competition?

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:31.510
I've withdrawn from it.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:35.180
No way! Are you really OK with that?

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:40.730
I have no right to say something like that to him.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:47.730
I'm the one that's trying to run away from the competition.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:54.260
You're not even good for killing time as you are now.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:59.680
You aren't going to let me have any fun, are you?

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:16.720
Yunoki is going to England?

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.210
Is that true?

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.160
I haven't heard anything about that.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.070
I don't really know if it's true or not.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:24.230
But if you look at that...

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:33.110
What shall we live for if Yunoki-sama is no longer with us?

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:36.540
Mai-san, Akira-san, I've decided.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:42.860
If Yunoki-sama is going someplace far away, I will follow him wherever he may go!

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.190
And we will accompany you, Towako-san!

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:48.800
Right now the rumor about Yunoki is all over the Music Department.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:53.390
If he'll be studying abroad, that means he won't be coming back to Japan for now.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:58.160
That's really cold of Yunoki. He didn't even tell you.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.000
That's not true.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.540
I think Yunoki has his reasons.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:04.820
Kazuki?

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:09.830
And I haven't told Yunoki about Kaho-chan yet, either.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.090
Kaho-chan.

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:16.040
Hihara-sempai.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:22.040
I see. You didn't know about him studying abroad, Hihara-sempai.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:26.460
Yeah. I realize it's not a problem I can help solve, though.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.080
But I wish he would have said something to me about it.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.550
Hihara-sempai...

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:34.510
I'm sorry!

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.360
You really had a tough time at the third selection.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.490
But I didn't even notice.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:42.440
No...

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.480
Are you OK?

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:52.530
I have something I'd like to talk to you about, Hihara-sempai.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:58.330
Hino? Nope, she hasn't come here.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.450
I see.

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:05.130
What's up? You came to me looking like you're expecting the worst.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.930
Well, there's a lot of stuff going on.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:11.150
If she didn't come, then never mind.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.750
A lot of stuff, huh?

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:18.510
You've really got a lot of burdens on your shoulders, don't you?

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:23.530
Just loosen up a bit and take things more at ease.

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:26.730
If you do that, those wrinkles on your brow will disappear.

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:31.060
Thank you, Kanayan.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:43.610
What the heck am I doing, sneaking around like that?

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:46.390
So, what is it you want to talk about?

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:50.050
I'm thinking of quitting the violin.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:53.270
You don't like playing the violin anymore?

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:02.680
If you really want to quit, I think you should.

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:07.610
Sorry, I made you hear something painful.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:16.630
Kaho-chan is quitting the violin.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:33.590
No, it's different now!

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:37.620
Kaho-chan...

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:43.280
That's not what I had to say to you!

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:53.630
Yunoki.

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:55.350
Hihara?

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:02.890
Oh yeah! There's this shop I want to go to. How about we go after school?

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:06.370
Kaho, are you sure about this?

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:08.700
Fuyuumi-san is worried about you.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.220
Fuyuumi-chan is?

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:12.580
Oh, I see. That's my bad.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:17.740
How was Fuyuumi-chan doing? Heh, it seems I'm more worried about her.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:21.760
Did you hear he was studying abroad?

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.450
Yunoki-sempai is going to England.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:28.720
Oops... It seems the story about me studying abroad has already spread around.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.200
So it was really true.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:33.130
And so you came to ask me yourself?

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:37.380
Yeah. I wanted to hear it directly from your mouth, Yunoki.

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:39.970
I wasn't trying to hide it.

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:44.600
I just didn't want to talk about it until everything was finalized.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:50.310
And you have a thing or two that you're keeping secret from me after all, Hihara-sempai.

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:55.480
Hihara?

00:11:56.350 --> 00:12:00.520
I wonder how long it's been since we stopped being able to be honest with one another?

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:07.740
Considering basic harmonics, depending on the acoustic properties of the instrument,

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.630
you can get the fundamental, first harmonic...

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:12.440
Hihara!

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:13.620
Class isn't over yet!

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:15.900
Ah, I'm sorry!

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:22.080
I realize you're busy with the competition, but you can't let your studies slip.

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:24.460
You want to continue studying music in college, right?

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:26.630
Well then, let's see...

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:31.790
Continue on with music in college... What does that even mean?

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:37.300
I was thinking I'd like to continue playing music for as long as I enjoyed it...

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:39.580
But, Kaho-chan...

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:44.530
Kaho-chan's smile disappeared as she turned to music seriously.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:49.380
If it's only because I like music, I'll come up against a wall someday.

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:54.820
The 3rd harmonic is...

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:06.140
Hino-sempai.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:08.600
Will she come today?

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:46.730
I'm searching for a sound.

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:49.760
A sound? What do you mean?

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:52.750
I wonder...

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:58.990
I'm playing like I normally do, but it just won't come.

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:04.640
Searching for a sound... Are you talking about the pursuit of the ideal tone?

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.420
Hino-sempai...

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:14.100
I want to see Hino-sempai.

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:15.220
Hino?

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:20.460
They ideal tone is far away from me, isn't it?

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:28.250
I wonder why I want to hear Hino-sempai's sound so much?

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:30.060
Hino's sound...

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:36.320
The Ave Maria you played with her during the retreat...

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:38.520
It was wonderful.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:42.110
That's right.

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:46.700
Back then, Hino's sound enchanted my heart.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:47.900
I'll never forget that.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:54.700
Why was it so enchanting?

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.890
Tsukimori-sempai?

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.800
Man, how did it get like this?

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.720
Did someone slack off from taking out the trash?

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.300
Hey, are you OK?

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:20.500
Sorry, my bad.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:24.420
Kanazawa-sensei.

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:28.670
And this is the last one.

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:33.070
And with that, I'll finish up my work and head on home.

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:39.070
What's the matter?

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:43.160
Did you finally realize how handsome I am?

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:45.440
Kanazawa-sensei.

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:49.260
Do you have some time?

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:00.280
Hihara-kun.

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:02.470
Osaki-sempai.

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:05.380
What is it? Did something happen?

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.870
Not something... More like...

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:14.570
Kaho-chan said she was quitting the violin.

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:17.240
Hino-san said that?

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:19.520
I don't really understand the reason.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:25.270
It's just that even if I asked her why, I wouldn't be able to do anything to help.

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:28.260
Hino is...

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:34.790
I think I'm going to withdraw from the competition.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:39.300
So you're next after Yunoki, huh?

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:42.140
So this is what Tsuchiura meant...

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:44.150
Huh?

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:46.770
Oh, just talking to myself.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:48.860
Or so I should be.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:55.200
So, has a new door opened for you?

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:03.560
Have you found something new, which is why you are withdrawing from the competition?

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:27.020
If you leave without finding a new door opened for you, it'll be difficult for you.

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:29.700
Sensei?

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.450
Just sayin'!

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:35.430
You probably wouldn't understand yet.

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:36.980
Just speaking in general of course.

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:42.640
Even if you quit now, the fact that you did your best won't change.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.620
Sensei...

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:50.520
If it's you, I'm sure you'll find a new door to open in no time.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:54.790
It's so nice being young...

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:14.390
Kahoko Hino.

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:15.880
Lili.

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:18.800
Are you really going to withdraw from the competition?

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:23.150
It's impossible for me now.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:26.500
After all, you can't fix the violin, right?

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:34.590
Perhaps the magic that was sealed inside the violin was destroyed when the strings broke.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:40.450
And it's now become just a normal violin.

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:42.640
A normal violin?

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.760
Are you really going to quit playing the violin?

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:50.140
I can't play it.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.840
But...

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:56.590
And you know, I'm a little relieved.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:02.710
If I quit playing the violin, I won't have to continue lying to everyone.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.410
I won't have to continue deceiving anyone.

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:10.620
That's why. Do you understand, Lili?

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:31.100
Tsukimori-kun.

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:40.790
What's the matter?

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:46.660
Is it true that you're quitting the violin?

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:51.330
How did you find out?

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.210
Are you OK with that?

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:59.170
It's not whether I'm OK with it or not, and it's not like I started this because I wanted to...

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:01.500
Stop lying to yourself.

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:04.760
I saw you on the road in front of the train station a while ago.

00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:12.950
Back then you were moving your fingers over a violin that no one could see, as if you adored it.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.320
That was...

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:19.970
You love the violin, don't you?

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:28.120
A long time ago, I broke one of my fingers.

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:35.150
It was in middle school. I got mixed up with some upperclassmen.

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:40.400
I was scared. Not of the upperclassmen.

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:44.200
But of the thought of not being able to play the violin again.

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:48.260
"I'll make it so you can never play the violin again."

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:51.060
That voice still rings in my ears.

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:55.070
A horror, bore straight into my heart.

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:58.560
Tsukimori-kun.

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:03.490
Can you go on without playing the violin?

00:21:05.390 --> 00:21:09.120
Can you bear not playing the violin?

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:10.250
I...

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:13.100
Your fingers, your heart...

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:16.810
If they never play the violin again, will they really be OK?

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:18.460
I'm fine!

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:21.520
I'm not interested in classical music.

00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:23.200
And even the violin...

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:25.430
Even the violin...

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:27.760
I don't even like playing the violin!

00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:33.730
Then why is it that you are crying?

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:41.840
Aren't those tears what you are really feeling?

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:46.610
No... I'm... It's not like that!

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:47.940
Hino...

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:52.120
Hino...

00:21:58.780 --> 00:22:02.960
Where are your true feelings?

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:39.640
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:39.860 --> 00:23:45.040
The names attached to the great works of the past and present, east and west, all have different origins.

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:51.010
The symphony that Schubert left only halfway complete is called his "Unfinished Symphony."

00:23:51.010 --> 00:23:56.570
And a symphony that Hayden wrote to shock the audience is called his "Surprise Symphony."

00:23:56.570 --> 00:23:58.310
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:58.310 --> 00:24:05.510
Of the Beethoven Symphonies "Eroica," "Fate," and "Pastoral," which one did he name himself?

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:09.480
You made a girl cry.

00:24:09.480 --> 00:24:10.800
I can't have that, now.

00:24:11.040 --> 00:24:12.760
I must apologize at once,

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:14.870
and ask the woman to forgive me.

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:17.810
Next episode: A Tear-colored Rondo.

00:24:18.460 --> 00:24:20.060
She made me cry as well.

00:24:20.380 --> 00:24:23.550
The answer is... "Pastoral!"
